1
00:00:25,254 --> 00:00:31,057
Hi from Tokyo again

2
00:00:31,057 --> 00:00:35,522
this is my second week back in Tokyo

3
00:00:37,412 --> 00:00:42,613
one thing I’ve noticed since coming back

4
00:00:42,613 --> 00:00:47,964
is that there definitely a lot more people

5
00:00:51,710 --> 00:00:59,018
I heard over tourism have been an issue

6
00:00:59,018 --> 00:01:04,972
so this week I’m trying to explore the quieter neighbourhoods of Tokyo

7
00:01:08,868 --> 00:01:14,036
starting off, we’re at Nippori

8
00:01:14,036 --> 00:01:20,156
from here we’ll be walking to Yanaka Ginza

9
00:01:21,494 --> 00:01:27,631
which is a traditional area of Tokyo

10
00:01:27,631 --> 00:01:33,969
filled with traditional wooden houses, izakaya and retro coffee shops

11
00:01:43,121 --> 00:01:46,883
you can also find local restaurants, sweets and handicrafts store 

12
00:01:50,144 --> 00:01:53,405
the area is also well known for it’s senbei

13
00:01:53,405 --> 00:01:57,469
you can smell the fresh senbei walking past

14
00:02:04,961 --> 00:02:09,861
lunch is at this kissaten

15
00:02:16,316 --> 00:02:21,601
this cafe is well over 70 years old

16
00:02:21,601 --> 00:02:28,139
I recommend making a reservation, since they have a no waiting policy

17
00:02:29,761 --> 00:02:34,544
but luckily it wasn’t too busy when I went

18
00:02:34,544 --> 00:02:39,779
I got a melon soda and their egg sandwich set

19
00:02:39,779 --> 00:02:44,645
this is a must get at this store

20
00:02:57,890 --> 00:03:07,455
this was the most fluffy egg and the bread was somehow chewy

21
00:03:07,455 --> 00:03:16,620
I would come back just for this sandwich

22
00:03:30,249 --> 00:03:39,330
time to look around more of the neighbourhood

23
00:03:39,330 --> 00:03:46,771
there are also a lot of craft stores in the area

24
00:04:01,555 --> 00:04:08,143
they have such a cute selection of things

25
00:04:19,482 --> 00:04:26,606
but there is one area I wanted to check out 

26
00:04:32,793 --> 00:04:42,978
here you can find a collaboration of small shops and cafes in and old traditional household

27
00:04:42,978 --> 00:04:50,269
starting with this craft beer store

28
00:04:54,550 --> 00:05:01,055
there are also a few art-craft shops

29
00:05:12,912 --> 00:05:19,083
and a bakery that sells bread and sweets

30
00:05:31,140 --> 00:05:38,381
this fig and chocolate one sounds so good

31
00:05:38,381 --> 00:05:45,639
grabbed a few so that I can have them for breakfast

32
00:05:50,873 --> 00:05:56,492
I was going to get some coffee here but the cafe was closed for today

33
00:05:57,429 --> 00:06:01,292
so we’ll continue our walk to the main area of Yanaka

34
00:06:07,613 --> 00:06:11,309
Yanaka is also interestingly known as the ‘Cat town’

35
00:06:17,798 --> 00:06:21,677
not quite sure why but there are so many cat themed shops here

36
00:06:35,957 --> 00:06:43,315
they have good coffee and brunch options

37
00:06:46,543 --> 00:06:50,975
the coffee was great as usual

38
00:06:50,975 --> 00:06:56,460
the staff are always super friendly and welcoming too

39
00:07:05,473 --> 00:07:13,634
the cafe also has some homewares and goods for sale

40
00:07:30,725 --> 00:07:37,030
this is the main Yanaka shopping street

41
00:07:37,030 --> 00:07:42,264
definitely a must visit for any cat lovers

42
00:07:55,124 --> 00:08:02,148
I think you can find some fun souvenirs here as well

43
00:08:07,132 --> 00:08:16,597
how cute are these chopstick holders

44
00:08:37,701 --> 00:08:43,471
and of course some Kiki merch

45
00:09:04,726 --> 00:09:09,224
getting one more treat before heading off

46
00:09:09,224 --> 00:09:13,506
there’s so many options

47
00:09:14,241 --> 00:09:18,138
but can’t go wrong with the original

48
00:09:20,362 --> 00:09:25,162
let’s go grabs some dinner

49
00:09:41,283 --> 00:09:47,169
the flagship store in Asakusa is huge

50
00:09:55,932 --> 00:10:01,584
another food I missed the most is definitely sushi!

51
00:10:24,110 --> 00:10:30,867
highly recommend this broccoli prawn salad

52
00:10:30,867 --> 00:10:36,703
it doesn’t look that promising but it’s really yummy

53
00:10:49,145 --> 00:10:55,232
and the corn tempura is really good as well

54
00:11:23,595 --> 00:11:31,187
late night snack time watching Bridgerton

55
00:11:31,187 --> 00:11:35,786
couldn’t wait this morning to try my carrot cupcake

56
00:11:48,997 --> 00:11:54,365
best way to end the night

57
00:12:05,319 --> 00:12:09,984
trying my fig and chocolate bread

58
00:12:14,516 --> 00:12:19,132
preparing some yogurt while I toast that up

59
00:12:20,804 --> 00:12:24,768
got some frozen mangos the other day

60
00:13:09,770 --> 00:13:15,873
this was such a good combo

61
00:13:15,873 --> 00:13:20,623
the weather is so clear today

62
00:13:24,101 --> 00:13:31,142
so we’re going to go check out another cute neighbourhood in Tokyo

63
00:13:38,617 --> 00:13:43,082
did I choose this place for the name?

64
00:13:43,450 --> 00:13:46,828
maybe...

65
00:13:50,841 --> 00:13:54,454
but they are also well known for their coffee

66
00:14:04,287 --> 00:14:09,555
they hand-pick their own original beans and roast them twice

67
00:14:09,555 --> 00:14:13,769
resulting in a really smooth and refreshing taste

68
00:14:30,425 --> 00:14:36,077
love this magazine for cafe recommendations 

69
00:14:38,653 --> 00:14:45,292
the area we’re going to check out today is Kuramae

70
00:14:46,195 --> 00:14:52,382
which is considered the 'Brooklyn' of Tokyo

71
00:14:58,988 --> 00:15:04,440
the area is known for its artisan community

72
00:15:04,440 --> 00:15:10,611
and is home to small manufacturers and craft stores

73
00:15:13,771 --> 00:15:18,504
this stationery shop is popular for their customisable notebooks

74
00:15:18,504 --> 00:15:23,671
you can customise everything from the cover to which paper you want

75
00:15:34,107 --> 00:15:39,241
they also had some other stationaries 

76
00:15:43,973 --> 00:15:50,077
they were also giving out this map of the area

77
00:15:50,077 --> 00:16:03,573
it showed all the fun shops and restaurants to visit

78
00:16:03,573 --> 00:16:09,576
so let’s go visit some of these shops

79
00:16:15,145 --> 00:16:20,496
this is both a cafe and a chocolate factory

80
00:16:27,922 --> 00:16:32,086
these would be such great presents

81
00:16:32,086 --> 00:16:37,554
and everything is made in house

82
00:16:50,330 --> 00:16:55,247
they have so many hot chocolate options

83
00:17:01,083 --> 00:17:06,401
I got the Kuramae hot chocolate

84
00:17:11,602 --> 00:17:17,807
there’s a huge line if you want to sit inside the cafe

85
00:17:17,807 --> 00:17:24,864
so I’m enjoying it at the park just outside

86
00:17:25,449 --> 00:17:31,386
it’s definately a lot richer than normal hot chocolates in Japan 

87
00:17:38,175 --> 00:17:42,757
this is partly a cafe

88
00:17:42,757 --> 00:17:46,604
but also a shop for handmade leather accessories

89
00:17:55,166 --> 00:17:58,945
this shop had some interesting incense and candles

90
00:18:10,919 --> 00:18:15,183
theres even a shop that specialises in masking tapes

91
00:18:15,183 --> 00:18:18,913
they have all different kinds of colours and patterns

92
00:18:24,783 --> 00:18:29,883
last shop for today

93
00:18:40,787 --> 00:18:45,753
how cute is this reusable coffee filter

94
00:18:58,563 --> 00:19:03,630
dinner is omurice

95
00:19:06,356 --> 00:19:14,852
I got the mushroom omurice

96
00:19:29,852 --> 00:19:33,765
today we’re headed to Tsukiji markets

97
00:19:34,769 --> 00:19:39,752
I heard it’s super crowded lately

98
00:19:42,227 --> 00:19:47,528
but there were a few shops I wanted to check out in this area

99
00:19:48,398 --> 00:19:53,565
starting with this viral coffee shop

100
00:20:00,790 --> 00:20:07,295
I came around 11 and thought the line didn’t seem too bad

101
00:20:07,295 --> 00:20:15,222
but there is only 1 barista and 1 staff working

102
00:20:15,222 --> 00:20:20,122
so the line ended up taking 1.5 hours

103
00:20:21,460 --> 00:20:27,129
which is more than I would usually be willing to wait for coffee 

104
00:20:27,129 --> 00:20:32,263
but the staff were really friendly despite being so busy

105
00:20:32,263 --> 00:20:38,216
and the coffee was honestly really good

106
00:20:38,216 --> 00:20:44,872
the sweetness of the matcha balances really well with the bitter expresso 

107
00:20:44,872 --> 00:20:52,213
I would recommend coming right at opening to avoid the crowd

108
00:20:52,213 --> 00:20:58,000
we were originally going to eat at the fish markets

109
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:05,508
but did not feel like lining up again

110
00:21:05,508 --> 00:21:11,228
I’ll come back next time

111
00:21:20,559 --> 00:21:25,141
but luckily there was another bakery I wanted to check out

112
00:21:25,141 --> 00:21:29,406
you can register online to get a wait time

113
00:21:35,208 --> 00:21:40,827
this bakery is where the famous salt bread originated

114
00:21:40,827 --> 00:21:44,741
they have so many options here

115
00:21:44,741 --> 00:21:49,222
I highly recommend trying the original shio pan and the mentaiko flavour 

116
00:21:49,222 --> 00:21:52,667
and the melon bread if you like something sweet

117
00:21:57,166 --> 00:22:03,303
they were still warm from the oven

118
00:22:05,979 --> 00:22:12,802
you can hear how crispy this is

119
00:22:15,160 --> 00:22:19,759
100% would recommend

120
00:22:19,759 --> 00:22:24,090
we just went shopping around Ginza afterwards

121
00:22:35,161 --> 00:22:41,114
in Shibuya for some dinner

122
00:22:41,532 --> 00:22:47,201
feels like ages since I last came here

123
00:22:56,232 --> 00:23:01,667
we’re at a all you can eat wagyu place

124
00:23:01,667 --> 00:23:06,701
they also have all you can eat side dishes

125
00:23:10,079 --> 00:23:14,962
and drinks

126
00:23:19,009 --> 00:23:23,072
the only downside is that you have to go to the counter to order everytime

127
00:23:52,087 --> 00:23:59,646
but the beef tongue was the best part

128
00:24:15,165 --> 00:24:21,955
it’s a rainy day here in Tokyo

129
00:24:25,065 --> 00:24:28,861
we’ll be exploring Kappabashi today 

130
00:24:34,413 --> 00:24:39,296
but need some caffeine first

131
00:24:39,296 --> 00:24:43,527
looks like hydrangea season is starting

132
00:24:44,230 --> 00:24:49,012
but that also means the start of rainy season

133
00:24:58,210 --> 00:25:05,200
the owner of this cafe used to work in New Zealand and Australia

134
00:25:05,200 --> 00:25:12,559
so I had high hopes for the coffee

135
00:25:17,341 --> 00:25:24,783
they were even playing a Australian radio station

136
00:25:27,910 --> 00:25:34,182
he seems to have won a lot of awards too

137
00:25:45,838 --> 00:25:51,306
the coffee was good as expected

138
00:25:51,306 --> 00:25:57,477
I can’t say no to a carrot cake

139
00:26:04,300 --> 00:26:08,598
this one was moist and not too sweet

140
00:26:22,077 --> 00:26:26,224
now time to look around Kappa street

141
00:26:29,903 --> 00:26:37,897
but do you know the story of the Kappa?

142
00:26:39,586 --> 00:26:44,920
they are these Japanese water yokais

143
00:26:44,920 --> 00:26:49,720
they look like a mix of a monkey and a turtle  

144
00:26:49,720 --> 00:26:55,088
with a bowl of water on it’s head

145
00:26:55,088 --> 00:27:00,473
they are known to be frightening creatures

146
00:27:01,041 --> 00:27:05,724
that pull victims under water to drown them

147
00:27:06,677 --> 00:27:10,757
but they have one essential flaw...  

148
00:27:10,757 --> 00:27:16,427
and it’s that they are extremely polite

149
00:27:17,597 --> 00:27:25,524
so if you bow to them they will bow back spilling the bowl of water on it’s head

150
00:27:26,377 --> 00:27:33,886
this will rendered completely helpless 

151
00:27:38,267 --> 00:27:44,956
but the street itself is well known for it’s kitchenware

152
00:27:44,956 --> 00:27:52,080
you can get some Japanese kitchenware at a really good price

153
00:27:53,652 --> 00:27:58,703
they had so many unique designs

154
00:28:02,047 --> 00:28:05,409
if you want to find cute plates and bowls I would highly recommend this place

155
00:28:14,907 --> 00:28:18,402
the whole street is lined with these stores

156
00:28:36,330 --> 00:28:41,363
had some great finds here

157
00:28:45,343 --> 00:28:52,551
dilemma between matcha or another coffee 

158
00:29:03,321 --> 00:29:12,619
matcha has really been taking over recently

159
00:29:12,619 --> 00:29:21,030
spending the afternoon doing some reading

160
00:29:38,356 --> 00:29:45,312
heading to Shimokitazawa today

161
00:29:45,312 --> 00:29:53,122
this area is well known for it’s vintage stores, cafes and bars

162
00:30:10,815 --> 00:30:16,116
nooooo

163
00:30:17,755 --> 00:30:24,127
the coffee shop I wanted to go to seems to be closed

164
00:30:32,237 --> 00:30:37,204
but good thing one of my favourite coffee shops was nearby

165
00:30:42,622 --> 00:30:46,937
always a good coffee here

166
00:30:47,890 --> 00:30:58,108
it’s definitely ice coffee weather now

167
00:30:59,596 --> 00:31:04,948
really needed this coffee

168
00:31:06,955 --> 00:31:12,507
time for some thrifting

169
00:31:17,156 --> 00:31:23,728
I feel like I always look around the same few shops when I’m here

170
00:31:43,745 --> 00:31:53,010
trying on a few dresses

171
00:32:20,620 --> 00:32:27,409
lunch menu is soup curry

172
00:32:32,945 --> 00:32:39,065
there seems to be a lot of soup curry places in this area

173
00:32:55,036 --> 00:33:05,371
you can customise everything from the spiciness to all the toppings

174
00:33:30,221 --> 00:33:43,834
soup curry was one of my favourite foods I tried in Hokkaido

175
00:33:52,279 --> 00:34:01,326
this one came pretty close

176
00:34:13,618 --> 00:34:17,916
back to shopping

177
00:34:26,444 --> 00:34:31,210
there are also a lot of cute stores like this in the area

178
00:34:33,836 --> 00:34:40,174
needed another coffee

179
00:35:25,627 --> 00:35:30,879
one of the main reasons I came here was to check out the record stores

180
00:35:37,049 --> 00:35:41,230
I’ve been thinking of getting a record player recently

181
00:35:42,601 --> 00:35:45,628
and I heard Japan is the best place to buy secondhand vinyls

182
00:35:52,819 --> 00:36:01,114
this place had such a big range

183
00:36:03,054 --> 00:36:10,144
was honestly a bit overwhelmed with where to start

184
00:36:28,005 --> 00:36:37,186
this place was better organised

185
00:36:38,306 --> 00:36:44,711
and had some newer records as well

186
00:37:07,906 --> 00:37:13,274
time to get some dinner

187
00:37:19,244 --> 00:37:25,147
we’re back in Asakusa area

188
00:37:26,184 --> 00:37:31,034
didn’t know the back streets had so many restaurants and bars

189
00:37:41,519 --> 00:37:46,152
my friend recommended this place for kushikatsu

190
00:37:54,229 --> 00:37:59,179
all the food was so good and affordable

191
00:38:01,470 --> 00:38:07,005
the fried natto was the best

192
00:38:09,664 --> 00:38:17,340
hope you guys enjoyed my second week here in Tokyo

193
00:38:18,628 --> 00:38:22,307
see you in the next video :)

